    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0605" n="535" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg535"/>

                <head>No. 314.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Schuyler.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 5,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I herewith inclose a copy of a
                        dispatch,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d315-f1"/> No. 147, of the 2d ultimo,
                    received from Mr. Heap, chargé at Constantinople, in which he informs the
                    Department of the release from imprisonment by the Sultan, at the request of Mr.
                    Wallace, of five Greeks.</p>
                <p>You may inform the Greek Government of the facts, as evincing the friendship of
                    the United States for that country.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d315-f1" n="*" xml:id="d315-f1-content">
                <p>See Mr. Heap to Mr. Frelinghuysen, No. 147, December 2, 1882, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
